Exports could include:

CSV
JSONL
HTML gallery
PDF specimen sheet later
Markdown shortlist

## 19. Relationship to Font Generator System

The Font Library System is the foundation for the future Bespoke Font Generator.

It provides:

Source font inventory
License tracking
Base font candidates
Style tags
Project collections
Known good typography examples
Font pairing records
Usage history
Training or transformation candidates

Before generating new fonts, the system should know which existing fonts are already available and which gaps still remain.

The font generator becomes necessary when the library reveals repeated gaps, such as:

A font is almost right but not sharp enough
A font has the right mood but wrong numerals
A font has the right structure but wrong serifs
A project needs a distinct custom type system
A drawn glyph needs to become part of a full font
A hybrid of several fonts would solve the design problem

## 20. First Version Scope

The first version should focus on immediate usability.

## Font Library v0.1

Required features:

Scan local font folder
Identify `.ttf` and `.otf` files
Extract basic metadata
Detect or attach license files
Generate quick previews
Generate alphabet sheets
Create manifest
Create static HTML gallery
Allow manual tags in a simple data file
Allow favorites in a simple data file
Export a shortlist

Not required in v0.1:

Full AI tagging
Full web app
Automated legal analysis
Font generation
Font transformation
Advanced pairing engine
Kerning analysis
Custom glyph ingestion

## 21. Success Criteria

The v0.1 system is successful if it can:

Scan the font collection
Create a trustworthy manifest
Render previews for the fonts
Show the fonts in a browsable gallery
Track license status
Let the user identify favorites
Let the user create project shortlists
Make the 1,800 fonts meaningfully easier to use

## 22. Strategic Value

The Font Library System converts a raw asset pile into a creative infrastructure layer.

Instead of having 1,800 fonts sitting in a folder, the user gains:

Searchable typography inventory
Licensing clarity
Project based font selection
Reusable visual identity decisions
Better brand consistency
Faster asset creation
A foundation for future font generation

This is the right first step because it creates immediate value while also preparing the ground for a more advanced Bespoke Font Generator later.

## 23. Key Insight

The font generator is not necessary simply because more fonts are possible.

The font generator becomes necessary when the font library reveals specific creative gaps.

Therefore the Font Library System should come first.

It helps answer:

What do we already have?
What is actually useful?
What can be safely used?
What fits the current projects?
What gaps keep appearing?

Once those gaps are visible, the Bespoke Font Generator can be built around real creative demand instead of abstract possibility.
